      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has:\n- Dozens of unused imports (ChronoField statics, serialization classes, etc.)\n- Several unused constants (`YEAR_STANDARD`, `YEAR_LEAP`, `STANDARD_YEAR_LENGTH`, `LEAP_YEAR_LENGTH`, `PARIS`)\n- The actual focused test is just 3 lines but buried under all this clutter\n\nI'll create a cleaned-up version with only necessary imports/constants and a clearer comment on the test intent.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed ~40 unused imports and 5 unused constants, and added a brief Javadoc on `test_getLong_null` explaining why a null field must trigger `NullPointerException`."
